EXP-02 emit-stage baseline, measured 2026-11-03 from the four arms' exp02_arm.log
================================================================================

METHOD. Each origin's draw phase is announced by a tqdm bar '[Origin N/13] Drawing
Posterior Samples', which carries no timestamp of its own. The log DOES carry 118
line-anchored timestamps and 431 in total, so each origin is attributed the nearest
PRECEDING timestamp in the text. The span origin_1 -> origin_13 is divided by 12.

WHY THE ATTRIBUTION IS EXACT RATHER THAN APPROXIMATE: the character distance from the
attributed timestamp to the origin marker is 227-228 chars for EVERY origin of EVERY
arm -- i.e. it is always the same preceding log line (the stage banner). A varying gap
would mean varying error; a constant gap is a fixed offset of well under a second.

arm                           span(min)   min/origin   attribution gap
----------------------------------------------------------------------
ctlfullzero_fortythree             41.3         3.44         227 chars
upctwofullzero_fortytwo            20.4         1.70         228 chars
upctwofullzero_fortythree          28.9         2.41         228 chars
ctlfullzero_fortytwo              182.2        15.18         228 chars

BASELINE: 1.70 - 3.44 min/origin, viz OFF, three arms.

EXCLUSION, stated rather than silent: ctlfullzero_fortytwo is EXCLUDED at 15.18
min/origin. Its pod was co-tenanted -- host load 43-66 throughout against 2-6 on the
other three, ~10% of CPU in nice'd processes that were not ours, GPU showing no
throttling of any kind (2407 of 2415 MHz, 30C, no HW/SW slowdown flags) and disk at
701 MB/s. The arm is sound; its wall clock is not a property of the run.

WHY THIS DISAGREES WITH A tqdm-ELAPSED PARSE (~1.25 min/origin): the bar's elapsed
field times the drawing loop ALONE. Each origin also does post-draw work -- metrics,
parquet writes -- which falls between one bar's end and the next bar's start. Wall
clock between origin starts is the cost; the bar is a component of it.

WHAT THIS IS FOR: the denominator the diagnostics probe is judged against. The
builders assert '~28 min/origin' for diagnostics-on in five docstrings and zero
measurement files. Against 1.70-3.44 that is an 8-16x increase on the emit stage,
not a doubling of the arm -- which is the difference between ~$3 and ~$23 over eight
arms. The probe's origins 1-2 replace the docstring with a number.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION, views-hydranet session, 2026-11-03
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reparsed from the same four logs with a separately written parser. All four spans and
per-origin figures reproduce EXACTLY: 41.3/3.44, 20.4/1.70, 28.9/2.41, 182.2/15.18.

The constant attribution gap also reproduces, under the method as stated -- the FIRST
'[Origin N/13]' marker of each origin sits 227 chars (fortythree) or 228 chars (the
other three) after its attributed timestamp, identical for all 13 origins of each arm.

A first attempt here read the gap over EVERY occurrence of the marker and found
227-34,314 chars, and briefly treated that as refuting the claim. That was wrong: tqdm
redraws the bar thousands of times per origin (2,830 and 4,302 markers in the two arms
checked) and only the first redraw is what the method attributes. The spread is an
artifact of measuring something the method does not use.

ALSO CORRECTED HERE: this session previously asserted that exp02_arm.log "carries no
per-line timestamps at all" and withdrew the baseline on that basis. The log carries
118 line-anchored timestamps and 437 by the count used here. The claim was false, and
it was reached from a grep whose output had been truncated to a file that was never
opened -- i.e. a conclusion drawn from unread output, which is the same failure as
describing an artifact one has not read. The withdrawal is itself withdrawn.
